    "https://account.jobs.ac.uk/jobs-by-email/": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "Login / Register - jobs.ac.uk This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Sign In Register Sign up today and get the latest jobs straight to your inbox with our Jobs by Email service.\n                        Once you are registered, you can manage your job alerts and easily turn on/off your alerts. If you are looking to advertise a job advert with jobs.ac.uk , please get in touch via the contact form or by phone.\n                        All contact is through our friendly team , rather than a recruiter self-service account. Email Password Stay signed in Forgotten your password? Create your jobs.ac.uk account by completing the form below. All personal data you provide in order to create your account is processed in accordance with our Privacy Notice First Name Last Name Email Password Confirm Password I have read and accept the Terms and Conditions I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Company News I would like to receive email communication from jobs.ac.uk relating to Conferences, Meetings & Events You can withdraw your consent for the communications above at any time by editing your profile or clicking the relevant unsubscribe link in any emails received. Help with your jobs.ac.uk account Are you having trouble signing in? jobs.ac.uk makes use of cookies to keep you logged in. If you\n                            do not have cookies enabled in your browser you may find you are\n                            unable to log in. For more details please see our Privacy Policy . Not receiving our emails? Our emails might have been incorrectly identified as Junk so\n                            please try checking your Junk folder if you have one. Then please\n                            add the following email addresses to your safe list or address\n                            book to ensure emails sent from us get through to you: jobsacuk.noreply@jobs.ac.uk jobsbyemail@jbe.jobs.ac.uk Different Problem? Please visit our Jobseekers Help page to contact us or view our FAQs to help you resolve your issues quickly and easily. Verify your Account We have sent a new verification email to .\n            Please check your email account now and click on the link in the email to complete your registration. If the email doesn't arrive within the next 10 minutes you may need to check your junk or spam folder. To help ensure our emails reach your inbox please add jobsacuk.noreply@jobs.ac.uk to your safe list or email address book. Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026"
    },
    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/about/": {
      "title": "This site uses cookies to store information on your computer.",
      "description": "jobs.ac.uk | About us This site uses cookies to store information on your computer. Some of these cookies are essential, while others help us to improve your experience by providing insights into how the site is being used. For more detailed information about the cookies we use, please see our Cookie policy I Accept Cookies I Do Not Accept Cookies Necessary Cookies Necessary cookies enable core functionality such as page navigation and access to secure areas. The website cannot function properly without these cookies, and can only be disabled by changing your browser preferences. Functional Cookies These help us to personalise the website to you by remembering your preferences and settings. functional On Off Marketing Cookies Marketing cookies help us provide personalised and relevant services or advertising to our website visitors, and to assess the effectiveness of our marketing campaigns. marketing On Off Analytics Cookies Analytical cookies help us to improve our website by collecting and reporting information on its usage. analytics On Off About this tool (Opens in a new window) Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters About Us Welcome to jobs.ac.uk - the leading international job board for academic, research, scientific, and professional careers. jobs.ac.uk was created in 1998 as a cost effective alternative to print media. Since its inception, jobs.ac.uk has grown and expanded its reach and services, evolving into a global hub for academic, research and professional job listings. We now advertise a huge range of vacancies from Professorships to Scientists, Research Associates to PhD studentships, and professional positions for a wide range of clients in the education, public and commercial sectors. jobs.ac.uk has become a trusted resource for job seekers looking for opportunities in universities, colleges, research organisations, and other academic institutions. We have been working with jobs.ac.uk for several years, they provide a platform for us to reach an international audience. The team is helpful and knowledgeable, supporting us in attracting and recruiting the best talent. Helen Johnson, Senior Appointments and Apprenticeship Manager, University of Oxford Growth at jobs.ac.uk In the modern world, being visible online is essential, which is why we have a dedicated web development and SEO team, working to keep the site optimised, compatible with ever changing algorithms, tracking interactions, and constantly improving the user experience whilst fulfilling customer requirements. We offer a wide range of products and services to enhance job listings and reach highly educated and talented jobseekers. 120 million user interactions 1 28.8 million page views 1 900k apply clicks 1 255k social media followers 95k jobs advertised 2 80% of top universities advertise with us 3 83% would consider working abroad 95% have a degree, masters or doctorate 1 GA4 data (12-month estimate based on 9 May - 9 July 2022) 2 jobs.ac.uk data 1 August 2021 - 31 July 2022 3 QS World University Rankings Work Experience Higher Education 67% Publicly Funded Organisation 9% Commercial Business 8% Not for Profit / Charity 5% None of the above 4% Further Education 4% Self Employed 3% How do we help jobseekers? We offer a free jobs by email service, meaning each job is emailed directly to targeted individuals actively seeking opportunities. We also have a dedicated career advice section which is updated regularly with articles to help throughout the job seeking process. Career advice is filled with useful information on how to find and apply for jobs, create the perfect CV, prepare for interviews, deal with nerves and unexpected questions, and ultimately how to succeed. How is jobs.ac.uk different from other job boards? What sets us apart from our competitors is our personal approach, all adverts are uploaded by a dedicated team of highly trained inputters, which provides a personal and value-added touch that sets us apart from other platforms. Also, all revenue generated by jobs.ac.uk is invested in education and research. What our clients say about us jobs.ac.uk has been our go to job board for many of the vacancies we recruit for across UKRI including the Science and Technology Facilities Council and Medical Research Council.  The site drives lots of traffic and generates high quality candidates for us.  The service we receive has always been of high quality and we look forward to continue working with a great team. Nicola Ashall, Resourcing Specialist Lead, UKSBS We are pleased to have been working with jobs.ac.uk for several years, they provide a platform for us to reach an international audience. The team are helpful and knowledgeable in developing this further through enhanced adverts and campaigns supporting us in attracting and recruiting the best talent to join the University. Helen Johnson, Senior Appointments and Apprenticeship Manager, University of Oxford The team at jobs.ac.uk have provided a first-class service from day one. As a new HE institution entering the sector, they immediately understood our recruitment needs and supported us in attracting high-caliber talent. The blend of targeted email and relevant marketing campaigns has been very effective, and we’ve always been able to count on jobs.ac.uk for their flexible approach and proactive engagement throughout. Fraser Tidman, Corporate HR Officer, UA92 (University Academy 92 Manchester) jobs.ac.uk are easy to work with and are quick with responses to our requests. Aimee Constantinou, HR Services Manager, The Francis Crick Institute I have worked with jobs.ac.uk for a number of years, and particularly with our Account Manager Emily, initially we worked together to find an advert package suitable for advertising our various opportunities at the Turing, including Fellowships, research engineering, studentships and business team roles. I’ve found jobs.ac.uk always responsive and proactive to work with and advertising with jobs.ac.uk attracts a high level of candidates to our roles. Emily and the team also provide key stats and useful job performance insights helping us make the most of our annual package. Francesca D’Amore, Recruitment Business Partner, The Alan Turing Institute We have seen positive and cost-effective results when recruiting to academic, research and professional services roles through jobs.ac.uk. The service has provided us with quick and easy access to millions of quality global HE candidates. Andrew Rowland, Resourcing Adviser, University of Cambridge Working with jobs.ac.uk is always a pleasure, the service is quick, efficient and effective.  They are always happy to advise on the best approach for senior and hard to fill roles and their knowledge of the HE sector is exceptional. Caroline Milligan, HR Business Partner Talent & Recruitment, University of Southampton jobs.ac.uk is our first choice platform for recruiting all of our academic and professional support vacancies.  The team at jobs.ac.uk provide a fast, friendly and efficient service and help us attract high-calibre applicants at a very cost-effective price. Simon Booth, HR Administrator, University of Bolton jobs.ac.uk has been our primary go to platform for recruiting all our academic staff for a couple of years now. Their international audience and global reach help us attract the right kind of high-calibre candidates to fill in even our niche academic positions which are quite hard to fill otherwise. Their team has provided exceptional customer service from day one and are extremely efficient and helpful, especially when we have urgent requirements. They have never failed to deliver with utmost promptness and a friendly approach especially Yunlong Zhao and William McArthur. Both of them are amazing to work with and super reliable. I hope to continue working with jobs.ac.uk for many more years in the future and wish them all the success and recognition which they truly deserve. Nazia Rehman, Human Resources Advisor, UOWD - University of Wollongong Dubai Searching and recruiting academics to teach and research in Borneo is never an easy task but jobs.ac.uk has never failed to help us find people interested in our unique experience. They are highly supportive, responsive and effective in delivering high quality applicants. We have tried many other search platforms but none has delivered as good as jobs.ac.uk. Yunlong’s kind gesture to visit us in Miri, Sarawak says a lot about the jobs.ac.uk outreach and his effort alone of travelling to Miri through multiple connecting flights truly shows that they care. Servia Gindi, Human Resource/Staffing Management, Curtin University - Malaysia We’ve been working with jobs.ac.uk for a long time. Every year we post new job ads and we appreciate mutual successful cooperation. We find the jobs.ac.uk a very useful recruitment tool. Diana Alken, HR Manager, KIMEP University “Professional!” We’ve worked with jobs.ac.uk since 2014, and they’ve consistently impressed me with their excellent guidance. When we were not sure of which products to select, they came up with an effective mixture of a couple of products. When we had difficulty writing an ad, they shared us with some successful examples. To sum up, they are professional. We look forward to working with jobs.ac.uk for many more years to come! Nayeon Lee, International Student Advisor, The Graduate School of Korean Studies, The Academy of Korean Studies Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job About Us Contact Us Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Terms of use Privacy Policy Cookie Policy Accessibility Statement Copyright © jobs.ac.uk 1998 - 2026 IE11 Trigger Browser Upgrade Recommended jobs.ac.uk has been optimised for the latest browsers. For the best user experience, we recommend viewing jobs.ac.uk on one of the following:"
    },
